<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating geometric probability using areas of shapes</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A chicken wanders randomly around a square yard with side length <b>{@s@} m</b>. It is equally likely to be at any point in the yard at any moment.</p>
<p>The farmer has drawn a circle of radius <b>{@r@} m</b> centred in the middle of the yard. There is also a small rectangular corner pen located at the top right, with a width of <b>{@w@} m</b> and a height of <b>{@h@} m</b>.</p>

[[jsxgraph width="400px" height="400px"]]
var s = {#s#};
var r = {#r#};
var w = {#w#};
var h_pen = {#h#};

var brd = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [-1.5, s + 1.5, s + 1.5, -1.5],
    axis: false, grid: false, showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}
});


var yard = brd.create('polygon', [[0, 0], [s, 0], [s, s], [0, s]], {
    fixed: true, fillColor: '#e0e0e0', fillOpacity: 0.5, 
    borders: {strokeWidth: 2, strokeColor: '#424242'},
    vertices: {visible: false}
});


var center = brd.create('point', [s/2, s/2], {fixed: true, visible: true, name: '', size: 2, color: '#0d47a1'});
var circle = brd.create('circle', [center, r], {
    fixed: true, fillColor: '#bbdefb', fillOpacity: 0.7, 
    strokeWidth: 2, strokeColor: '#1976d2'
});


var pen = brd.create('polygon', [[s-w, s-h_pen], [s, s-h_pen], [s, s], [s-w, s]], {
    fixed: true, fillColor: '#ffe0b2', fillOpacity: 0.8, 
    borders: {strokeWidth: 2, strokeColor: '#f57c00'},
    vertices: {visible: false}
});


brd.create('text', [s/2, -0.6, s.toString() + ' m'], {fixed: true, anchorX: 'middle', anchorY: 'middle', fontSize: 14, strokeColor: '#424242'});
brd.create('text', [-0.6, s/2, s.toString() + ' m'], {fixed: true, anchorX: 'middle', anchorY: 'middle', fontSize: 14, strokeColor: '#424242', display: 'internal', rotate: 90});
brd.create('text', [s/2, s/2 - r*0.4, 'circle'], {fixed: true, anchorX: 'middle', anchorY: 'middle', fontSize: 14, strokeColor: '#0d47a1'});
brd.create('text', [s - w/2, s - h_pen/2, 'pen'], {fixed: true, anchorX: 'middle', anchorY: 'middle', fontSize: 14, strokeColor: '#e65100'});


brd.create('segment', [[s/2, s/2], [s/2 + r, s/2]], {fixed: true, strokeColor: '#1976d2', strokeWidth: 1});
brd.create('text', [s/2 + r/2, s/2 + 0.3, r.toString() + ' m'], {fixed: true, anchorX: 'middle', anchorY: 'bottom', fontSize: 12, strokeColor: '#1976d2'});
[[/jsxgraph]]

<p><b>a) </b> What is the total area of the yard?</p>
<p>\(\text{Total Area} =\) [[input:ans1]] \(\text{m}^2\)</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> What is the exact area of the circular region? <i>(Leave your answer in terms of \(\pi\). Type <b>pi</b> to enter \(\pi\)).</i></p>
<p>\(\text{Circle Area} =\) [[input:ans2]] \(\text{m}^2\)</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>

<p><b>c) </b> Since the chicken is equally likely to be anywhere, what is the probability that at a random moment the chicken is inside the <b>circular region</b>?</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as an exact fraction involving \(\pi\). Type <b>pi</b> to enter \(\pi\)).</i></p>
<p>\(P(\text{inside circle}) =\) [[input:ans3]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>
<p><b>d) </b> Find the probability that at a random moment the chicken is in <b>neither</b> the circle <b>nor</b> the pen. <i>(Type <b>pi</b> for \(\pi\).)</i></p>
<p>\(P(\text{neither}) =\) [[input:ans4]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: Total Area</b><br>
The yard is a square with side length \(s = {@s@}\) m. The area of a square is \(s^2\).</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\text{Total Area} = {@s@} \times {@s@} = {@ta1@}\text{ m}^2\)</p>

<p><b>Part b: Favourable Area</b><br>
The circular region has a radius \(r = {@r@}\) m. The area of a circle is \(\pi r^2\).</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\text{Circle Area} = \pi \times {@r@}^2 = {@r^2@}\pi\text{ m}^2\)</p>

<p><b>Part c: Geometric Probability</b><br>
Geometric probability is calculated as the ratio of the favourable area to the total area:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P = \frac{\text{Area of favourable region}}{\text{Total area}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(\text{inside circle}) = \frac{{@r^2@}\pi}{{@ta1@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P = {@ta3@} } \)</p>
<p><b>Part d: Neither region</b><br>The circle and the pen do not overlap, so the area that is in the circle <em>or</em> the pen is \({@r^2@}\pi + {@w*h@}\). The chicken is in neither region with the <strong>complement</strong> of that probability:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(\text{neither}) = 1 - \frac{ {@r^2@}\pi + {@w*h@} }{ {@s^2@} } = {@ta4@} \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
